WEBVTT

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.280
<i>Minamoto!</i>

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.280
<i>Minamoto!</i>

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.870
<i>It's Minamoto.</i>

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.260
<i>Minamoto!</i>

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.540
What was that... just now?

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.820
That's Minamoto.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.340
Since his debut race, he's had 6 wins out of 6 races.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.520
I knew he was overwhelmingly fast, but there's a huge difference.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.700
<i>As always, Minamoto is...</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.490
<i>No.  He's more spirited today.</i>

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.580
<i>Taira!</i>

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.160
<i>Is it because Taira's here?!</i>

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.000
<i>You look happy, Naomi.</i>

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.960
He's got a time within the 43-second range already!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.680
He's two whole seconds faster than Ishihara.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.610
If he carries on getting these times right after he starts driving,

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.640
our ace is going to be completely overshadowed.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.060
That Naomi.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.230
If he carries on driving at that speed from the start, he'll wear the machine out.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.140
Maybe we should call him back into the pits.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.040
No.  There's no need.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.810
He must really want to drive.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.020
Huh?

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:31.290
There are times when drivers have this urge to drive that they can't hold back.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.120
That calm Naomi is trying to show us a different face.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.040
Don't you want to see what it's like?

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.550
<i>Just like Shiba said.</i>

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.140
<i>He's ridiculously fast.</i>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.970
<i>He's probably three seconds faster than me in each lap.</i>

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.220
<i>One second in a race is different from one second in normal life.</i>

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.370
<i>The machine will go tens of meters in a second.</i>

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.420
<i>If there's a three-second gap, the difference is...</i>

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.130
<i>This is the difference between my skills and his.</i>

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.080
<i>Minamoto showed me this at the very start...</i>

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.210
<i>Telling me to "hurry and catch up"!</i>

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.350
43.228 seconds.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.350
He's shortened his time by 0.6 seconds all of a sudden.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.780
Naomi is kinda scary today.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.120
Ryou's also quickened his pace!

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.340
He got within the 45-second range along with Taira.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.810
Ryou's more experienced in the FSte, after all.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.550
He can't lose.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.060
But if they continue driving so close together, they may start fighting it out.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.940
And this is still a free run.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.760
Should we put out a sign so he'd put more distance in between?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.400
Let Ryou also be, huh?

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.370
1 minute 45.814 seconds!

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.860
Hey, isn't this...

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.320
It's 0.06 seconds faster than Komazawa's best time on this circuit!

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.470
That's good.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.830
He's not doing so badly.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.290
Now then, I'll just quickly—

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:55.690
You think he's okay?

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.860
He was rather agitated.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.890
Of course he would be.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.390
Capeta beat his best time all of a sudden, after all.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.870
You gotta be kidding me!

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:11.950
If I get beaten by a guy in his first race, there's no place for me!

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:21.210
<i>I have a year's experience.</i>

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:25.160
<i>I'll show him my experience and strength!</i>

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.470
Naomi, 1 minute 43.406 seconds!

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:49.600
Ishihara, 1 minute 44.781 seconds!

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:58.110
Shiba, 1 minute 45.092 seconds!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.290
<b>1 minute 45.834 seconds!</b>

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:14.450
All right.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.360
You're in the 45-second range.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.500
You're doing well, Noriko.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.540
<b>How about Taira?</b>

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:21.800
Taira is...

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.010
45.814 seconds.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.950
Komazawa, 1 minute 45.806 seconds!

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.660
Capeta, 1 minute 45.799 seconds!

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.320
Amazing.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.790
Everyone's times are going down.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.920
It's because Minamoto posted a great time at the start.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.460
Everyone's influenced and they're quickening their pace.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.820
<i>It's not just Minamoto.</i>

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.530
<i>Ryou is also serious.</i>

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:08.180
<i>Until now he's been crushed by Minamoto, but Taira's rekindled his fire.</i>

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.190
Shiba, 1 minute 44.693 seconds!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:18.190
Capeta, 1 minute 45.002 seconds!

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:22.040
Naomi, 1 minute 43.248 seconds!

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.410
<i>You really look happy.</i>

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.250
<i>Naomi...</i>

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.340
<i>you must have been waiting for this day.</i>

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.980
<i>Since that day you first met him at that kart circuit 6 years ago,</i>

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:43.010
<i>you were waiting for the day to fight Capeta-kun head-on.</i>

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.550
<i>I'm Minamoto Naomi.</i>

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:48.300
<i>You are?</i>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.950
<i>T-Taira Capeta.</i>

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.230
<i>Fight to your heart's content.</i>

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.230
<i>And give it all you got.</i>

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.940
<i>And then he's sure to respond to you...</i>

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.400
<i>Capeta will.</i>

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:07.080
<i>I won't lose.</i>

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.870
<i>I'm gonna catch up to him no matter what!</i>

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.960
Thank you, everyone!

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.050
Bye-bye!

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.670
See you again!

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.760
Good job.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.220
Thanks.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:29.400
Your CDs are selling well because you work so hard on your promotion campaign.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.060
The manager of this store asked if you could do it again tomorrow.

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:34.060
Umm... tomorrow is...

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.440
I know.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.700
The race, right?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.800
It's okay.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.530
I've opened time for you in the afternoon.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.780
I'm sorry for being selfish.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.490
You've worked hard, so it's your reward.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:49.490
But I'll have you work hard in the morning to make up for it.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:52.410
Yes, yes.  I know.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.420
<i>I'll come no matter what.</i>

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:03.300
<i>I can't miss this.  It's Ca-chan and Minamoto's first battle.</i>

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.030
All right!  He's in the 43-second range.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.800
It's really amazing.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:15.270
His best time in the audition was somewhere around the 45-second range?

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:20.020
The tune-ups for the school and racing machines are totally different.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:24.980
The machines don't look different from each other, but that's how it is, huh?

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.700
But the major difference is...

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.700
<i>his</i> presence.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.960
42-second range?!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.220
And just when we thought Capeta shortened his gap to within a second...

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.930
Taira's awakened the eyes of the monster.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.970
Oh, Tanaka-san.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.850
What's the matter?

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.360
We received a fax from Italy.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.070
From Italy?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.530
It looks like it's urgent.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.950
<b>Practice is over.</b>

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.670
The results are as expected.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.510
Minamoto Naomi got the top time.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.750
He's the only one in the 42-second range,

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.630
and the only thing you can say is, "As expected."

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.100
If he keeps this up in the qualifier, there'll be no one challenging him for pole position.

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:35.920
2nd is Ishihara.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.430
3rd is Shiba.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.800
As always, Sam's dominates the top three.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.400
But what gets my attention is Shiba's time.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:51.030
1 minute 44.236 seconds is his best time on this course.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:55.030
It isn't inferior to Ishihara's time; 1 minute 44.208.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.660
This is his 6th race in the FSte and he's finally gotten used to his machine.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:00.850
Maybe Shiba's finally showing his true strength.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.210
Speaking of true strength...

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:09.630
This is Taira's debut race.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:14.220
With 1 minute 44.471 seconds,
he's in 4th place, following Shiba.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:19.180
He suddenly beat the ace,
Komazawa, so that's quite impressive.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:24.230
Of course I was expecting something like that.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.210
That was incredible, Capeta.

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:27.480
You're in 4th place.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.950
You did great.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.320
How about Minamoto?

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.240
1 minute 42.901 seconds.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:36.990
42 seconds?!

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.910
Well, he's special.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.910
I'm still behind by 1.5 seconds.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.370
Damn it!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.760
Komazawa-san.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.220
I won't lose in the qualifier!

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.700
You're in 8th place out of 18 cars.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.340
This is your first time in the top 10 this year.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.310
You did great.

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:09.220
I did great?!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.070
When I lost to Taira, who drove in the FSte for the first time today?!

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:14.580
I don't want to lose against him, no matter what.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.740
I lost to him at the school.
I don't want to lose in the real race, too!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.210
Minamoto.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.800
44-second range, huh?

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.770
I thought you could do better than that.

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.720
I'm not satisfied either.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.460
The fight is from here.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.940
I'll shorten that 1.5-second difference.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.640
Do your best.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.220
I heard you called for me.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.250
Yeah.  We called you.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.430
Your mother will join us later.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.000
My mother?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.750
What's this about?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.600
The thing is...

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:25.060
You're going to leave for Italy right now.

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.670
The Formula Euro team in Modena is saying they want to test you.

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:35.280
The meeting is on Sunday, at 10 a.m. local time.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:39.010
There's an eight-hour time difference, so you'll make it if you leave now.

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:41.240
We've already got the flight tickets ready.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:43.990
That's the only business.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:44.700
Go straight away.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:49.710
What's the matter?

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.880
There's still something I need to do.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:54.590
"Need to do"?

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.450
Don't tell me you're talking about tomorrow's race.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:00.600
Don't worry about the team.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:06.560
Ishihara and Shiba will probably rejoice because they'll now have a chance to win.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:16.480
Could it wait until I finish the qualifier at least?

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:17.570
Can't I do that?

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:18.950
The qualifier?

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:22.030
You're not going to race in the finals,
 so why do you want to race in the qualifier?

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:23.960
I want to race.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:24.740
No matter what.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:26.540
Naomi.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.500
No, I won't allow it!

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:35.980
I don't know what this is all about, but you should quickly throw away your boring obsession.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:39.420
You won't get another chance like this in the world of motor sports!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:49.390
You may be fast in Japan, but there are plenty of drivers like you out there in the world.

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:53.350
It's not just you who's on that team's list.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:57.580
If you refuse this offer, they'll contact another driver.

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:02.530
You'll be cast aside and the driver called in your place will climb the steps to the next stage.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.910
If that happens, we have no business with you!

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:11.030
The ones who get up to the F1 are those who take these chances.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.200
You can't make it there just because you're fast.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:19.450
If you really want to go to the F1,
don't let go of a chance in front of you.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:22.160
If you get acknowledged in the Formula Euro,

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.800
the chance of you driving in the European F3 will also open up.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:31.430
And if you put up a result there,
the authorized people in the F1 will notice you.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:36.400
Your fastest route into the F1 has just opened up.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.110
You walk that path straight!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:44.780
Let's go, Naomi.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:53.710
<b>The qualifier for the 6th race in the Formula Stellar series has now begun.</b>

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:59.980
<b>The starting grid for tomorrow's final will be decided by the best time in this qualifier.</b>

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:06.140
<b>Each car will drive out into the fierce 15-minute time attack, in the hope of getting a higher grid position.</b>

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.200
<i>I won't lose either!</i>

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.610
Do your best, Capeta.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:27.990
Hey, Nobu-kun.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:30.260
What's wrong with Sam's machine?

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:39.500
Car #8.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.450
It's Minamoto's machine.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.210
Yeah, it is.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.700
Do you think there's some trouble?

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:47.060
When there are a lot of machines on the course it's hard to get a clear lap.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.780
It may be his plan to wait until there's an opening, but...

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.900
<i>Minamoto...  Why aren't you coming out?!</i>

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.580
<i>Too bad, Taira.</i>

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:08.110
<i>When you finally caught up and came to the FSte, Minamoto got away from you again.</i>

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.570
<i>But for me, this is a chance.</i>

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.040
<i>After Minamoto left for Italy, I remembered again.</i>

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:17.500
<i>That we're directly connected to the F1.</i>

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.250
<i>If I leave a result here, I can go out into the world.</i>

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.960
<i>For that reason, I'm going to win!</i>

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.340
<i>Why aren't you coming out, Minamoto?!</i>

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.020
Course out!

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.230
Damn it!

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.470
We're going to call him back in straight away.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.580
If sand gets into the radiator, the engine will burn out.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.420
Yes.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.380
What?!

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.270
Is that... true?

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:00.420
Is that... true?

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:01.390
Yeah.

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:05.880
Sam's Team officially announced Minamoto's absence just now.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.470
No way.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:11.380
<i>Not again.</i>

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.550
<i>Just when we thought we caught up, he puts more distance between us.</i>

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.780
<i>We're repeating ourselves.</i>

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.730
Minamoto went to Italy?!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.830
Yeah.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:23.730
Apparently he had an offer from a Formula Euro team for a test drive.

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:31.400
<i>Capeta's been chasing his back for these past six years...</i>

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.900
<i>And when we thought he could finally fight him today...</i>

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:41.920
Why?!

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.980
<i>Do your best.</i>

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.080
<i>He got away again.</i>

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.520
There's three minutes left.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.560
If you get out there right now,
you can do one more attack.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:07.320
Go!

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.520
Three more minutes...

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.810
That's right!

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.820
The qualifier isn't finished yet!

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.700
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.710
<i>I have to do my race!</i>

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.930
<i>My job is to finish the race, stand out, and leave results!</i>

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.790
<i>Isn't that right, Nobu?!</i>

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.280
Tsubomaki-san!

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:26.560
Komazawa is...

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:29.710
He passed all sectors with top times and is now on the final corner!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:30.920
What?!

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:37.350
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.310
<i>I'll show them all how fast I am!</i>

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:43.310
<i>My fighting spirit won't lose to anyone!</i>

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:49.580
42.943 seconds!

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.410
That's incredible!  It's the top time!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.650
He passed Ishihara and Shiba in one go!

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:57.620
To think that he'd get a super lap like that...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:00.320
<i>See that?!</i>

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.080
<i>This is my true strength.</i>

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.290
<i>My fighting spirit is different from the others!</i>

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:53.440
He's at the top of the road I need to advance to.

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:54.940
It's not like I've lost sight of him!

00:22:55.690 --> 00:22:58.230
Before anything, I need to do my job.

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:00.820
The job I should be doing.

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:01.940
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:03.400
Second Driver!

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:05.070
Open up the future!
